			"color":"#232",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> / <Picture 1>: The lead female singer — a young woman with long wavy dark-brown hair, gold hoop earrings, a delicate gold chain necklace, wearing an elegant one-shoulder black draped gown with waist cutouts. Mic assignment: [Handheld Mic] — she grips a silver dynamic handheld microphone in her right hand for the entire performance; as long as she is lip-syncing, the mic must remain strictly positioned near her mouth in every shot.\n<Picture 2>: The environment — a vast indoor concert stage with a futuristic radial ceiling canopy, dense arrays of blue beam lights, glowing LED cube screens, a glossy mirror-like stage floor, and silhouetted audience heads in the foreground.\n<Picture 3>: The two backup dancers — wearing flowing green-to-white gradient tulle ball gowns with floral waist accents and curling vine-like green headpieces, performing fluid lyrical arm choreography.\n\nsummary:\nA 15-second cinematic ballad MV in which the elegant black-gowned singer <Subject 1> delivers a deeply emotional vocal at the heart of the blue-lit mega-stage <Picture 2>, while two green-tulle dancers <Picture 3> swirl around her in graceful support.\n\nretention_analysis:\nFaithfully retain the singer's facial features, wavy dark hair, gold jewelry and one-shoulder black cutout gown (<Picture 1>); the stage's radial ceiling structure, crisscrossing blue light beams, LED cubes and reflective floor (<Picture 2>); the dancers' gradient green gowns, floral headpieces and extended arm poses (<Picture 3>). Visual pacing follows gentle ballad grammar — slow dolly push-ins, smooth grounded steadicam arcs, rack focus and breathing handheld micro-motion — matched to the slow, lyrical emotional rhythm of the performance.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA high-end concert-ballad aesthetic drenched in deep blue volumetric beams, soft haze and mirror-like floor reflections; all camera work is strictly grounded (dolly track, handheld gimbal, steadicam walked by the operator at stage level), with an intimate, heartfelt performance tone.\n\n[Shot 1] A ground-level low-angle hero wide shot establishes the vast stage of <Picture 2>, blue beams fanning through haze; <Subject 1> stands center in her black one-shoulder gown, rim-lit, raising the silver handheld microphone to her lips; (S1) she opens the song with eyes gently closed, chest rising with a deep breath, delicate brow micro-expressions, the mic gripped tightly and held strictly at her mouth; the camera performs a slow dolly push-in toward her while the two dancers of <Picture 3> hold sculptural poses with arms extended at either side of the stage.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:04.000, the shot cuts to a medium close-up as the operator walks a smooth slow steadicam arc around <Subject 1> at ground level; a rack focus pulls from the silver mic grille to her glistening, dreamy eyes; (S1) she sings with half-lidded longing, lips parting in heartfelt articulation, subtle head sway on the breath, her free hand resting gently over her heart while the mic hand keeps the microphone firmly positioned near her mouth; blue beams sweep softly behind her wavy hair.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:08.000, the shot cuts to a stage-level sweeping pan: the dancers of <Picture 3> circle around <Subject 1>, their green gradient tulle skirts swirling in slow spirals, arms tracing lyrical overhead curves; <Subject 1> remains the center of the orbit, leaning slightly forward with trembling emotional breath, (S1) pouring out the rising verse with yearning eye contact toward the lens, the silver handheld mic never leaving her mouth; the glossy floor doubles the blue beams and the flowing green dresses in reflection.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:11.500, the shot cuts to an intimate close-up with a whisper-slow push-in and shallow depth of field, blue beam bokeh blooming behind; (S1) <Subject 1> delivers the emotional climax — a single shimmering tear-glint, furrowed yet serene brows, jaw relaxed into a sustained heartfelt note, gentle handheld camera breathing synced to her sway; her fingers remain wrapped around the mic body, the microphone strictly positioned near her mouth through the final held note as the blue lights slowly dim around her.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nReverberant indoor-arena ambience — a hushed crowd with occasional soft applause, faint fabric rustle of swirling tulle gowns, soft footsteps on the glossy stage floor, subtle mic-handling clicks and gentle breath intakes close to the mic capsule.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
